IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gp-dates`
IMPORT `gp-part4a`

-- Supreme Court Act 1986 (Vic), Part 4A -- the questions of the GROUP MEMBER.
--
-- SEAT: the person with a claim who is, or may be, a group member in a group proceeding (a class action) in the Supreme
-- Court of Victoria: "Can my claim be brought as a group proceeding?", "Am I a group member?", "By when must I opt out?",
-- "What happens to my limitation period?", "What costs can I be made to pay?", "How much of my recovery goes to the lawyers
-- under a group costs order?", "Must I be told?", "By when must I take the step the Court set, or claim from the fund?",
-- "Am I bound by the judgment?", "May I appeal if the plaintiff does not?". The representative plaintiff has a seat of their
-- own (gp-seat-plaintiff.l4). The Court and the defendant get none: the Court's findings, leave and orders are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, numbers, dates, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of gp-part4a.l4. The
-- two duties with a date (s 33ZG, s 33ZA(3)(c)) are DEONTIC rules run inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Supreme Court
