§ `Group proceedings: the group member's questions`

§§ `Bringing the claim as a group proceeding`

@export Can my claim, with others' claims against the same person, be brought as a group proceeding (class action) in the Supreme Court of Victoria (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33B, 33C, 33G)?
GIVEN `how many persons have claims` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons, counting you, have claims against the same person (company, government or individual)
      `same circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all those claims are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances
      `common question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all those claims give rise to a substantial common question of law or fact
      `kind of proceeding` IS A `Kind of proceeding` @desc What the proceeding is: a claim of any other kind (most claims for injury, loss or money), or one of the kinds Part 4A excludes (a proceeding under sections 34 and 35, about a deceased estate, about trust property, or under Order 18)
      `cross-vesting only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court would have jurisdiction over every one of the claims only by cross-vesting from another court's jurisdiction (rare; answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my claim be brought as a group proceeding` MEANS
    `s 33C -- a group proceeding may be commenced` `how many persons have claims` `same circumstances` `common question` `kind of proceeding` `cross-vesting only`

§§ `Being a group member`

@export Am I a group member in the group proceeding (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33A, 33E, 33J, 33KA)? Your consent is not needed, except for governments, Ministers, public bodies and judicial and other officers.
GIVEN `within the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you fall within the group of persons the writ describes (the people on whose behalf the proceeding was brought)
      `public person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the Commonwealth, a State or Territory, a Minister, a public-purpose body corporate (not an incorporated company or association), a judge or magistrate, or an officer acting as such
      `written consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have consented in writing to being a group member (needed only for the public persons above)
      `opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have opted out by notice in writing
      `reinstated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has reinstated you as a group member after you opted out
      `excluded by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered that you cease to be, or not become, a group member (for example for lack of connection with Australia)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a group member` MEANS
    `s 33A, 33E -- I am a group member` `within the group` `public person` `written consent` `opted out` `reinstated` `excluded by the Court`

@export What is the last day on which I can opt out of the group proceeding (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33J(2))? You opt out by notice in writing before the date the Court fixed.
GIVEN `opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court fixed (as extended, if it was) before which group members may opt out; it is in the notice of the proceeding
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I can opt out` MEANS
    `s 33J(2) -- the last day to opt out` `opt-out date`

@export Can I still opt out of the group proceeding today (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33J(2), (3))?
GIVEN `opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court fixed (as extended, if it was) before which group members may opt out
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still opt out today` MEANS
    `s 33J(2) -- I may opt out today` `opt-out date` `today`

@export My claim arose after the group proceeding began: can the group be altered to include me (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33K)?
GIVEN `leave given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has given the plaintiff leave to amend the writ to alter the description of the group
      `day my claim arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action accrued (usually the day you suffered the loss or injury)
      `day proceeding began` IS A DATE @desc The day the group proceeding was commenced
      `date fixed with leave` IS A DATE @desc The date the Court fixed when giving leave: causes of action accruing before it can be included
      `would have been included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would have been in the group (or, with your consent, would have been) had your cause of action accrued before the proceeding began
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the group be altered to include me` MEANS
    `s 33K -- the group may be altered to include me` `leave given` `day my claim arose` `day proceeding began` `date fixed with leave` `would have been included`

@export Must I act through a litigation guardian in the group proceeding (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33A, 33F)? You do not need one merely to be a group member.
GIVEN `under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18
      `incapable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are incapable, because of injury, disease, senility, illness or physical or mental infirmity, of managing your affairs in relation to the proceeding
      `taking a step` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you want to take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it yourself (rather than simply be a group member)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I act through a litigation guardian` MEANS
    `s 33F -- I must act by a litigation guardian` (`s 33A -- I am a person under disability` `under 18` `incapable`) `taking a step`

§§ `Limitation periods`

@export What does the group proceeding do to the time limit for suing on my claim (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZE)? Gives the new last day once the period runs again.
GIVEN `my claim is covered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a group member and your claim is one the group proceeding relates to
      `day proceeding began` IS A DATE @desc The day the group proceeding was commenced
      `my last day without it` IS A DATE @desc The last day you could have sued on your own claim had there been no group proceeding (from the Limitation of Actions Act 1958 or other law)
      `opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have opted out of the group proceeding
      `day I opted out` IS A DATE @desc The day you opted out (any day if you have not)
      `ended without deciding my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceeding, and any appeals, have been determined without finally disposing of your claim
      `day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day of that final determination (any day if it has not happened)
GIVETH A `My limitation period`
`What happens to my time limit` MEANS
    `s 33ZE -- my limitation period` `my claim is covered` `day proceeding began` `my last day without it` `opted out` `day I opted out` `ended without deciding my claim` `day it ended`

§§ `Costs`

@export What costs can I, as a group member, be made to pay (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33Q(3), 33R(2), 33ZD, 33ZDA)? An empty list means the Court may not order you to pay costs.
GIVEN `sub-group representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has appointed you (not being the plaintiff) the representative party of a sub-group
      `individual question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has permitted you to take part to decide a question that relates only to your own claim
      `group costs order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made a group costs order (legal costs as a percentage of what is recovered) in the proceeding
GIVETH A LIST OF `Costs a group member can be made to pay`
`What costs can I be made to pay` MEANS
    `s 33ZD -- the costs I can be made to pay as a group member` `sub-group representative` `individual question` `group costs order`

@export Under a group costs order, what are the total legal costs taken from the award or settlement (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZDA(1)(a))?
GIVEN `group costs order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made a group costs order in the proceeding
      `percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage set in the order (as amended, if it was), e.g. 25 for 25%
      `amount recovered` IS A NUMBER @desc The total amount of the award or settlement recovered in the proceeding, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What are the legal costs under the group costs order` MEANS
    `s 33ZDA(1)(a) -- the legal costs under the group costs order` `group costs order` `percentage` `amount recovered`

@export Under a group costs order, how much of my own recovery goes in legal costs and how much do I keep (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZDA(1)(b))?
GIVEN `group costs order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made a group costs order in the proceeding
      `percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage set in the order (as amended, if it was), e.g. 25 for 25%
      `shared by recovery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order shares the legal costs among the plaintiff and group members in proportion to what each recovers
      `my recovery` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you recover from the award or settlement before legal costs, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE `My share under a group costs order`
`How much of my recovery goes in legal costs` MEANS
    `s 33ZDA(1)(b) -- my share under the group costs order` `group costs order` `percentage` `shared by recovery` `my recovery`

@export Who must pay the defendant's costs if the group proceeding fails (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33ZD, 33ZDA(2))? Group members are not ordered to pay them except under ss 33Q and 33R.
GIVEN `group costs order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made a group costs order in the proceeding
GIVETH A `Who answers for the defendant's costs`
`Who pays the defendant's costs` MEANS
    `s 33ZD, 33ZDA(2) -- who answers for the defendant's costs` `group costs order`

@export How much of the damages awarded to the group may be paid to the plaintiff for costs the defendant does not pay (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZJ)?
GIVEN `damages awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has made an award of damages in the group proceeding
      `Court satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court, on the plaintiff's application, is satisfied that the plaintiff's reasonably incurred costs are likely to exceed the costs recoverable from the defendant
      `costs incurred` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs the plaintiff (or sub-group representative) reasonably incurred in the proceeding, in dollars
      `costs recoverable` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs the plaintiff can recover from the defendant, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of the damages may go to the plaintiff's costs` MEANS
    `s 33ZJ -- the most that may be paid out of the damages for the representative's costs` `damages awarded` `Court satisfied` `costs incurred` `costs recoverable`

§§ `Notices`

@export Must I, as a group member, be given notice of this matter (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33X, 33Y)? Notice is given as soon as practicable, in the manner the Court orders; not receiving it does not undo any step, order or judgment (s 33Y(7)).
GIVEN `matter` IS A `Matter for notice` @desc What the notice would be about: the commencement and the right to opt out; the defendant's application to dismiss for want of prosecution; the plaintiff's application for leave to settle the plaintiff's own claim; an offer to compromise; an application to approve a settlement or discontinuance; or any other matter
      `damages claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relief sought in the proceeding includes a claim for damages
      `dispensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has dispensed with notice of the matter
      `ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has ordered that notice of the matter be given
      `just without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a settlement or discontinuance approval: whether the Court is satisfied it is just to decide it without notice to group members
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I be given notice` MEANS
    `s 33X -- notice of the matter must be given to me` `matter` `damages claimed` `dispensed` `ordered` `just without notice`

@export Can the group proceeding be settled or discontinued without the Court's approval (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33V)? Answers whether it may be settled or discontinued.
GIVEN `approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has approved the settlement or discontinuance
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May the group proceeding be settled` MEANS
    `s 33V -- the group proceeding may be settled or discontinued` `approved`

§§ `After judgment or settlement (only if the Court has made an order setting a step or a fund)`

@export The Court set a step group members must take by a date to share in the relief or a payment: where do I stand (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZG)?
GIVEN `day of order` IS A DATE @desc The day the Court made the order setting the step
      `date in order` IS A DATE @desc The date the order specifies, after which a group member who has not taken the step is not entitled
      `step taken` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have taken the step (for example registered or lodged a form)
      `day step taken` IS A DATE @desc The day you took it (any day if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the step`
`Where do I stand on the step the Court set` MEANS
    `s 33ZG -- what became of my step` `day of order` `date in order` `step taken` `day step taken` `today`

@export What is the earliest last day for claims the Court can fix when it sets up a fund for group members (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZA(3)(c))?
GIVEN `day of order` IS A DATE @desc The day the Court made the order constituting the fund
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest last day for fund claims` MEANS
    `s 33ZA(3)(c) -- the earliest day the order may fix for claims` `day of order`

@export Is my claim for payment out of the group's fund in time, or allowed late (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZA(3)(c), (4))?
GIVEN `day of order` IS A DATE @desc The day the Court made the order constituting the fund
      `day fixed` IS A DATE @desc The day fixed by the order on or before which group members are to claim
      `claim made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made your claim for payment out of the fund
      `day of claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you made it (any day if you have not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `fully distributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund has already been fully distributed
      `late claim allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court, finding it just, has allowed you to claim after the day fixed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my fund claim in time or allowed` MEANS
    `s 33ZA(3)(c), (4) -- my claim on the fund is in time or allowed` `day of order` `day fixed` `claim made` `day of claim` `today` `fully distributed` `late claim allowed`

@export Am I bound by the judgment in the group proceeding (Supreme Court Act 1986 ss 33ZB, 33KA)?
GIVEN `member at judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a group member (within the group and not opted out or excluded) when the judgment was given
      `excluded since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Court has since ordered that you cease to be a group member and are taken never to have been one
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I bound by the judgment` MEANS
    `s 33ZB -- the judgment binds me` `member at judgment` `excluded since`

@export What is the last day I may appeal on behalf of the group if the plaintiff (or sub-group representative) does not (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZC(5))?
GIVEN `last day for representative` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time the rules of court allow the plaintiff (or, for sub-group questions, the sub-group representative party) to appeal
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I may appeal for the group` MEANS
    `s 33ZC(5) -- the last day I may appeal as representative` `last day for representative`

@export May I commence an appeal on behalf of the group today because the plaintiff (or sub-group representative) did not (Supreme Court Act 1986 s 33ZC(5))?
GIVEN `last day for representative` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time the rules of court allow the plaintiff (or sub-group representative party) to appeal
      `representative appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the plaintiff (or sub-group representative party) commenced an appeal within that time
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I appeal for the group today` MEANS
    `s 33ZC(5) -- I may appeal as representative today` `last day for representative` `representative appealed` `today`
